&lt;p&gt;Read the ‘Adventures in Publishing’ Report - &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140713055858/http:/bit.ly/VDoBX0" title="http://bit.ly/VDoBX0"&gt;http://bit.ly/VDoBX0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
View the Brand Perfect Tour Schedule - &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140713055858/http:/bit.ly/11McH46" title="http://bit.ly/11McH46"&gt;http://bit.ly/11McH46&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Read Condé Nast Executive Director’s Interview - &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140713055858/http:/bit.ly/YE7g2F" title="http://bit.ly/YE7g2F"&gt;http://bit.ly/YE7g2F&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Brand Perfect Tour is returning to New York City with two events to help demystify brand management in an age where publishers are communicating across multiple platforms: from print and digital publishing to tablets and smartphones. The events, &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140713055858/http:/brandperfect.org/index.php/component/events/?view=eventdetails&amp;amp;id=7"&gt;Design for Publishing&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20140713055858/http:/brandperfect.org/index.php/component/events/?view=eventdetails&amp;amp;id=6"&gt;Adventures in Publishing&lt;/a&gt;, are intended for senior management, designers and developers working in brands and agencies who want to sharpen their creative skills and deliver compelling cross-platform brand strategies.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>